  - "Changed [field] from [old] to [new]" in gray-800
  - Reason below in gray-500, smaller text
  - Timestamp right-aligned in gray-400, 12px
- Empty state: "No manual changes yet — using system defaults"

### STATE MANAGEMENT
Use React Context (BenchmarkProvider) wrapping the entire app:
- activeVertical: currently selected vertical ID
- overrides: object mapping vertical ID → custom benchmark values
- activeBenchmarks: derived from overrides[activeVertical] OR defaults
- updateThreshold(fieldPath, newValue, reason): merge override, log change
- resetToDefaults(): remove override for active vertical, log reset
- changeHistory: array of { id, timestamp, verticalId, fieldPath, oldValue, newValue, reason, changedBy }

### UPDATE DIAGNOSTIC ENGINE
Modify all diagnostic logic to read thresholds from useBenchmark().activeBenchmarks instead of hardcoded constants. When vertical changes:
- Recalculate all findings
- Update results header to show: "Diagnostic Results — [Vertical Name]"
- If sample data is loaded but from a different vertical, show a toast warning

### DESIGN REQUIREMENTS
- Follow existing Airtable-inspired clean design (white, gray-50, blue-600 accent)
